---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About — Motiva Hub" description="A sanctuary for the disciplined mind.">
  <section class="feed" style="padding-top: 140px;">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="kicker">About Motiva Hub</p>
      <h1 class="bp-title" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">A sanctuary for the <em>disciplined mind.</em></h1>
      <div class="about-body">
        <h2>Our Intent</h2>
        <p>Motiva Hub exists for the person who has grown tired of being inspired and is ready to be changed. We treat personal growth as a discipline, not a mood — the slow, unglamorous work of becoming someone worth being.</p>
        <p>We are an independent editorial project, built in the spirit of the great print magazines — quiet, deliberate, and allergic to noise. Our subjects are old ones: mindset, habit, discipline, attention, growth. They have guided disciplined minds for two thousand years; we simply translate them for the modern reader.</p>
        <h2>Four Principles</h2>
        <div class="pillars" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));">
          <div class="pillar" style="text-align: left;">
            <p class="pillar-word">On Stillness</p>
            <p>We begin where the noise ends. The first discipline is to create the quiet in which a thought can survive.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="pillar" style="text-align: left;">
            <p class="pillar-word">On Practice</p>
            <p>Ideas are cheap; practice is the only currency that compounds. We favour the unglamorous repetition over the brilliant intention.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="pillar" style="text-align: left;">
            <p class="pillar-word">On Time</p>
            <p>The day is the unit of a life well lived. We design the morning, protect the deep hours, and let the evening fall quietly.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="pillar" style="text-align: left;">
            <p class="pillar-word">On Failure</p>
            <p>The fall is data. We do not romanticise struggle, but we refuse to waste it — every setback is a map of the next attempt.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>